# R2-sort — the signature negative (rejection class R2, lara-core@0.2, issue #89)
#
# THE MOTIVATING EXAMPLE, LITERALLY. Before @0.2, `num_lt(sys_new, accuracy)`
# was a perfectly well-formed `Prop`: nothing in the core knew that `num_lt`
# compares numbers, that `sys_new` is a system, or that `accuracy` is a
# measurand. On a strict step `ord@1` caught it late, as an R13 replay
# rejection — a type error surfacing as an evidence failure. On a defeasible
# step nothing caught it at all.
#
# The declared signature in `ord-v1.policy.lara` says
#
#     pred num_lt(Num, Num)
#     con sys_new : System
#     con accuracy : Measurand
#
# so the leaf below is ill-sorted at argument 0 (`System` supplied where `Num`
# is declared) and again at argument 1 (`Measurand` for `Num`). `checkUnit`
# stage 2 rejects it as R2 at the earliest honest point, before any support
# term is read and before any backend is consulted.
#
# The example is deliberately built on the SHIPPED `ord-v1` signature rather
# than a bespoke one (#89 §7's merge gate): the point is that the corpus's own
# frozen vocabulary rejects this, not that a signature written for the occasion
# can be made to.
#
# Contrast:
#   * examples/R2 is the R12 (§8.1 Path-B) demonstration and is NOT this class.
#     The two names collide only because R2-the-directory predates
#     R2-the-executable-class; docs/rejection-surface.md carries the note.
#   * examples/S2 is the same artifact WELL-SORTED, and accepts.
#
# Expected verdict: reject R2.

artifact sort_demo at sha256:5252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252
policy ord-v1
use backends [ord@1]

# The claim states the ill-sorted atom directly, so the artifact is otherwise
# structurally impeccable: the support term concludes exactly the claim's
# formal target, so nothing upstream of stage 2 has anything to object to and
# the rejection is unambiguously about the signature.

claim c1
  nl      = "sys_new is numerically below accuracy"
  formal  = num_lt(sys_new, accuracy)
  binding = { author = alice, rationale = "A comparison written against the wrong two things.", audit-status = reviewed }

# The ill-sorted leaf: `num_lt` is declared over two `Num`s, and this applies it
# to a System and a Measurand. Every other declaration in this file is
# well-sorted, so the mutant is single-defect.

leaf e1 : num_lt(sys_new, accuracy)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/accuracy.md#row=sys_new]

arg a1 : supports(c1) by leaf(e1)

status c1
